  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 is the best RNA encoder (acc=0.520, F1=0.498), clearly outperforming pca_n2000 (0.485) and scgpt (0.411). Image-only with resnet50 is very weak (0.208), suggesting RNA dominates. All four completed experiments used singleprofile; multiprofile has not yet been tested. Question: Does multiprofile with avgpool aggregation improve upon the best singleprofile result (0.520) for scvi_n200? This is a clean single-variable change (singleprofile → multiprofile + avgpool) that isolates the effect of multi-profile aggregation. Choosing avgpool over transformer first is the more conservative test: if simple averaging of profiles helps, it confirms multiprofile is beneficial and justifies testing transformer next; if it doesn't help, transformer is less likely to. With 5 experiments remaining, this high-information experiment will guide whether to invest further in multiprofile or pivot toward multimodal fusion with a stronger image encoder (e.g., ViT-L)."
